{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795224,"nonce":"uttuYyjo9G2b9J44VOdf+Qyzj/U=","title":"Add YouTube broadcasts, channel selection and live chat as a provider","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P3\n\nScope\nImplement a YouTube provider with OAuth channel selection, supported broadcast/stream creation/binding/lifecycle, existing-broadcast selection and server-streaming live chat with continuation/reconnect and quota handling. Support users who configure their destination in OBS without giving extra provider control permissions. Keep account/channel/broadcast IDs distinct and adapt the UI to granted features.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nFixtures cover multiple channels, incomplete live eligibility, denied scopes, quota exhaustion, interrupted chat, ended broadcasts and uncertain start/stop responses. Retry does not create duplicate public events. Collaboration survives provider errors and no service/account secret reaches room clients or logs. Final provider review and quota requirements are recorded before release.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}